<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <a href="/obs/<%= team.id %>/connections" class="text-surface-400 hover:text-white text-sm inline-flex items-center gap-1 mb-4">
      <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Connections
    </a>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">OBS Agent Setup</h1>
    <p class="text-surface-400 mt-1">Run this on the PC that runs OBS — it connects out to the server, so no ports need to be open.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="glass-card rounded-xl p-6 mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1"><%= conn.name %></h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-surface-400 mb-4">Your agent token (keep it secret):</p>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
      <code id="agent-token" class="flex-1 bg-surface-900 border border-surface-700 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-sm text-brand-400 break-all"><%= conn.agent_token %></code>
      <button onclick="copyToken()" class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-brand-600 hover:bg-brand-500 text-white text-sm font-medium transition-colors">
        <i class="fas fa-copy mr-1"></i>Copy
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="glass-card rounded-xl p-6 mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-4">Steps</h2>
    <ol class="space-y-4 text-sm text-surface-300 list-decimal list-inside">
      <li class="space-y-1">
        <span>In OBS, go to <b>Tools &rarr; WebSocket Server Settings</b>, enable the WebSocket server, set a port (default 4455) and a password.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="space-y-1">
        <span>On the streaming PC, open a terminal and run:</span>
        <pre class="bg-surface-900 border border-surface-700 rounded-lg p-3 text-xs text-surface-300 overflow-x-auto">git clone https://github.com/voidlinedevelopment/production.git
cd production/agent
npm install
copy .env.example .env   # (Windows: copy .env.example .env)</pre>
      </li>
      <li class="space-y-1">
        <span>Edit <code>.env</code> — put your token in <code>AGENT_TOKEN</code>, and your OBS WebSocket password in <code>OBS_PASSWORD</code>:</span>
        <pre class="bg-surface-900 border border-surface-700 rounded-lg p-3 text-xs text-surface-300 overflow-x-auto">SERVER_URL=https://production.ocrp.cc
AGENT_TOKEN=&lt;paste your token&gt;
OBS_HOST=127.0.0.1
OBS_PORT=4455
OBS_PASSWORD=&lt;your obs password&gt;</pre>
      </li>
      <li class="space-y-1">
        <span>Start the agent and leave it running (OBS must be open):</span>
        <pre class="bg-surface-900 border border-surface-700 rounded-lg p-3 text-xs text-surface-300 overflow-x-auto">npm start</pre>
        <span class="text-surface-400">You should see <code>Registered as agent for OBS connection #...</code> then <code>Connected to OBS.</code></span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="glass-card rounded-xl p-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Then what?</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-surface-300">
      Go to the <a href="/obs/<%= team.id %>" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">OBS Control</a> page. The connection will show
      <span class="text-green-400 font-medium">Connected</span> once the agent is online, and you can switch scenes, start/stop the stream and recording from the website — no public IP or port forwarding needed.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  function copyToken() {
    const token = document.getElementById('agent-token').innerText.trim();
    if (navigator.clipboard) {
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(token).then(() => alert('Token copied!'));
    } else {
      const ta = document.createElement('textarea');
      ta.value = token;
      document.body.appendChild(ta);
      ta.select();
      document.execCommand('copy');
      document.body.removeChild(ta);
      alert('Token copied!');
    }
  }
</script>
